  "content": {
    "id": "p56-q13-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "Jimmy is given a function $y=f(x)$ and is instructed to transform it into $y=f(1-2x)$.\n\nDescribe a possible sequence of transformations so that Jimmy can obtain $y=f(1-2x)$ from $y=f(x)$, if the sequence must begin with a:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p56-q13-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "translation.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Translate left by 1, dilate horizontally by factor $\\frac12$, then reflect in the $y$-axis.",
          "worked": "Translate left by 1:\n$$y=f(x+1).$$\nDilate horizontally by factor $\\frac12$, replacing $x$ by $2x$:\n$$y=f(2x+1).$$\nReflect in the $y$-axis, replacing $x$ by $-x$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=f(-2x+1)\\\\y&=f(1-2x).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p56-q13-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "reflection.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Reflect in the $y$-axis, translate right by 1, then dilate horizontally by factor $\\frac12$.",
          "worked": "Reflect in the $y$-axis:\n$$y=f(-x).$$\nTranslate right by 1, replacing $x$ by $x-1$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=f(-(x-1))\\\\y&=f(1-x).\\end{align*}$$\nDilate horizontally by factor $\\frac12$, replacing $x$ by $2x$:\n$$y=f(1-2x).$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p56-q13-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "dilation.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Dilate horizontally by factor $\\frac12$, reflect in the $y$-axis, then translate right by $\\frac12$.",
          "worked": "Dilate horizontally by factor $\\frac12$:\n$$y=f(2x).$$\nReflect in the $y$-axis:\n$$y=f(-2x).$$\nTranslate right by $\\frac12$, replacing $x$ by $x-\\frac12$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=f\\left(-2\\left(x-\\frac12\\right)\\right)\\\\y&=f(1-2x).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      }
    ]
  },
